cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use the PocketGull Typeface Superfamily in clinical software, medical informatics, vision science research, or assistive reading systems, please cite it as below."
title: "PocketGull Typeface Superfamily: Optotypically Calibrated Clinical & Ophthalmological Vector Letterforms"
abstract: "PocketGull is an open-source clinical, ophthalmological, and telemetry monospace typeface superfamily bridging tactile humanist warmth with zero-error clinical precision. Engineered on a 1000 UPM grid with LogMAR 0.0 Snellen optotypic geometry, PocketGull incorporates 256 Unicode Braille patterns (U+2800..U+28FF), ISMP/FDA numeral disambiguation (slashed zero, curved lowercase l, serifed capital I), Louise Sloan 5:1 proportional legibility, 670nm Retinal Photobiomodulation (PBM) mode, and native multi-script support for Canadian Aboriginal Syllabics, Chinuk Pipa, Cherokee Syllabary, Neo-Tifinagh, Ethiopic Ge'ez, Adlam, Vai, and Pan-Tribal North American Indigenous orthographies under the CARE Principles for Indigenous Data Sovereignty."
